s:\n\n- Pick G ({3,4}) alone: covers 3 and 4. Then we have sets: H, C, B, G. Check duplicates: none. All elements covered exactly once. Good.\n\n- Pick A ({3}) and F ({4}) separately: covers 3 and 4 separately. Then sets: H, C, B, A, F. All distinct. Good.\n\n- Could we pick A and G? No, G already covers 3, so A would duplicate 3. Not allowed.\n\n- Could we pick F and G? G covers 4, so duplicate 4. Not allowed.\n\nThus subcase 1a yields 2 solutions.\n\nSubcase 1b: choose D ({2,3}) for element"}}],"created":1790951278,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4185,"total_tokens":4953,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-8raeQeLFMS3WNPfFynbTaaZcNtpAgGJa","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4185,"prompt_ms":517.695,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12370250896057348,"prompt_per_second":8083.910410569929,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2326.776,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0336062581486307,"predicted_per_second":329.6406701805417}}